{"id":"NCT06707090","title":"Tissue Repair Gel in Venous Leg Ulcers (US)","official":"A Phase 3 Randomized, Parallel Group, Double-Blind Study to Evaluate the Efficacy, Tolerability, and Safety of TR987® 0.1% Gel Versus Standard of Care in the Treatment of Chronic Venous Insufficiency Leg Ulcers (VLU)","summary":"The goal of this clinical trial is to learn if TR987 0.1% gel + Standard of Care works better than Standard of Care alone to treat Venous Leg Ulcers (VLUs). It will also provide additional information about the safety of drug TR987 0.1% gel.","conditions":["Venous Leg Ulcer","Venous Ulcer","Venous Stasis Ulcer","Venous Stasis","Wound Heal","Wounds","Venous Insufficiency of Leg","Non-healing Wound"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"TR987 0.1% gel + Standard of Care"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"Standard of care"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Adults 18 years and older\n* Venous insufficiency has been clinically diagnosed clinically and medically confirmed.\n* Females who are neither pregnant nor breastfeeding and if of child-bearing potential are on an acceptable method of birth control.\n* The Venous Ulcer should be between 2 cm2 and 12 cm2 at randomization.\n* Target ulcer age must be ≥ 4 weeks at Screening.\n* Participants must have adequate arterial flow as confirmed by ABI/TBI, TB, SPP, TCPo2, or Duplex Doppler.\n* Body mass index (BMI) ≤ 50 kg/m2.\n* HbA1C ≤12%.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Target ulcer has been treated with prohibited medications or therapies.\n* History of radiation at the target ulcer site.\n* Target ulcer decreases in area by 30% or more during screening period.\n* History of osteomyelitis at the target ulcer within 6 months of screening.\n* Participants considered nutritionally deficient.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":312,"start":"2025-01-28","pcd":"2027-12","upd":"2026-02-12","sponsor":"TR Therapeutics","areas":["other"],"central":["Anhthu Nguyen Vice President, Global Clinical Operations · (+61) 280 034 554 · anhthu.nguyen@trtherapeutics.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Clincial Research Site 21","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85715","s":"ANR","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":""},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 43C","city":"Castro Valley","pr":"California","zip":"94546","s":"R","lat":37.6941,"lon":-122.0863,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 14","city":"Fresno","pr":"California","zip":"93710","s":"R","lat":36.7477,"lon":-119.7724,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 11","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90063","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 43A","city":"San Francisco","pr":"California","zip":"94115","s":"R","lat":37.7749,"lon":-122.4194,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 43B","city":"San Francisco","pr":"California","zip":"94117","s":"R","lat":37.7749,"lon":-122.4194,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 54","city":"Vista","pr":"California","zip":"92081","s":"R","lat":33.2,"lon":-117.2425,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 47","city":"Deerfield Beach","pr":"Florida","zip":"33442","s":"ANR","lat":26.3184,"lon":-80.0998,"c":""},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 38","city":"Hollywood","pr":"Florida","zip":"33021","s":"NYR","lat":26.0112,"lon":-80.1495,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 40","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32209","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 19","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33150","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 26","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33156","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"info@trtherapeutics.com"},{"f":"Clincial Research Site 13","city":"Pembrook Pines","pr":"Florida","zip":"33026","s":"R